      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1197375849">
          <groundspeak:date>2023-09-26T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Write note</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP326 Penhold [DID NOT FIND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I mean, I found where it IS, but the cap is somewhere a loooong way down. “5 CM BGL”, lol. Probably not going to be logging this one any time soon. C’est la vie!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683818676">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP326 - Penhold - this one needs a longer shovel than we had! We got closer for the next finder! &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Road trip! Iron Phoenix and I had a fantastic caching and capping from Calgary to Red Deer.Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683662367">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP326 - Penhold&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time in Red Deer!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Well, after reading the previous logs, we figured we might need some help.  We stopped at the Home Hardware before getting to the location and bought a bucket.  I figured we could cut out the bottom &amp; use it as a bit of a tube to keep some of the sidewall dirt from caving in.  It might work great for the next person. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_blackeye.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;  We dug as deep as we could, but neither of us had the arm length needed.  We did the best we could and tried to leave it better/easier to dig than we found it so we have to go with what we got from it. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_blackeye.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682493550">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-30T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP326 Penhold.  Otherwise know as the big dig.  Dirt fills in as quick as remove in it.  Luckily someone had left an old survey stake to gauge how far down we had to go.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680984725">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="553001">Bearberrys Cub</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP326 Penhold

N 52° 08.204 W 113° 52.316&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headed out early this morning in less than ideal weather conditions for geocaching -- fog and rain/snow, to rendezvous with Trefoil/Voyager.  The plan was to head north as far as Lacombe, caching as we went.  This was the first of two brass caps we found today.  As we approached GZ, it was obvious that there had been a lot of excavation in search of this cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
    </groundspeak:cache>
